  "marketSentiment": "NEUTRAL",
  "macroTheme": "Nasdaq suffers worst week since June as 3.7% CPI, CoreWeave credit scare and Kospi circuit breakers trigger AI de-rating; Dow escapes with gain as rotation into defensives and energy accelerates. Hormuz attacks escalate — Brent back at $110. Gold stable at $4,165-4,181 as geopolitics offset rate headwinds. 10Y yield fell 15bp despite hot CPI — safety bid, not duration trade.",
  "macroOverview": "The week of 12-16 October 2026 was defined by a violent rotation out of AI-linked growth into defensives, energy and value. A hot 3.7% CPI print on Wednesday removed residual Fed-cut hopes and triggered the Nasdaq's worst week since June (-5.49%). Kospi circuit breakers tripped Thursday on Asian AI financing fears. CoreWeave credit scare compounded the chip rout: AMD -11%, AVGO -7.3%, NVDA -5.4%. The Dow gained 0.67% as UNH, WMT, HD and energy names carried. Brent tagged $110 (first time since May) as Iran stepped up Hormuz attacks — at least nine commercial ships hit. IEA released 20M barrels of diesel. WTI settled $101.41, up 10.4% on week. Gold remarkably stable at $4,181 (-0.8%). Silver crashed 5.5% to 57.305 as industrial-demand thesis broke. VIX surged 31.4% to 19.99. The 10Y yield fell 15bp to 5.09% — a safety bid into duration, not a growth trade. Mega-cap tech earnings loom.",
